 you can then choose one of the following formats: <ul><li><em>Generic file</em> displays links to the files and adds icons that symbolize the file extensions. If <em>descriptions</em> are enabled and have been submitted, then the description is displayed instead of the file name.</li><li><em>URL to file</em> displays the full path to the file as plain text.</li><li><em>Table of files</em> lists links to the files and the file sizes in a table.</li><li><em>RSS enclosure</em> only displays the first file, and only in a RSS feed, formatted according to the RSS 2.0 syntax for enclosures.</li></ul> A file can still be linked to directly by its URI even if it is not displayed.','','none'),(4635,_binary 'Flag to control whether this file should be displayed when viewing content','','none'),(4636,_binary 'The log entry explaining the changes in this revision.','','11.3.8'),(4637,_binary 'At least one authentication provider must be defined for resource @id','','none'),(4638,_binary 'At least one format must be defined for resource @id','','none'),(4639,_binary 'The ID of the shortcut.','','none'),(4640,_binary 'The UUID of the shortcut.','','none'),(4641,_binary 'The bundle of the shortcut.','','none'),(4642,_binary 'Weight among shortcuts in the same shortcut set.','','none'),(4643,_binary 'Route name','','none'),(4644,_binary 'The language code of the shortcut.','','none'),(4645,_binary 'Shortcut link','','11.3.8'),(4646,_binary 'Rebuild access','','none'),(4647,_binary 'The rebuild_access setting is enabled in settings.php. It is recommended to have this setting disabled unless you are performing a rebuild.','','none'),(4648,_binary 'Relate nodes to taxonomy terms, specifying which vocabulary or vocabularies to use. This relationship will cause duplicated records if there are multiple terms.','','11.3.8'),(4649,_binary 'Taxonomy term ID','','none'),(4650,_binary 'Taxonomy term name','','11.3.8'),(4651,_binary 'Return to site content','','11.3.8'),(4652,_binary 'Preferre