ry 'Overriding default settings','','none'),(5249,_binary 'Approving and managing comments','','none'),(5250,_binary 'This page provides a list of all comment types on the site and allows you to manage the fields, form and display settings for each.','','11.3.8'),(5251,_binary 'Administer comment types and settings','','11.3.8'),(5252,_binary 'Comment types','','11.3.8'),(5253,_binary 'Comment type settings','','none'),(5254,_binary 'Target Entity Type ID','','none'),(5255,_binary 'Comment type %label has been updated.','','none'),(5256,_binary 'Comment type %label has been added.','','none'),(5257,_binary 'The comment author\'s email address.','','11.3.8'),(5258,_binary 'Comment Type','','none'),(5259,_binary 'The comment type.','','none'),(5260,_binary '%label is used by the %field field on your site. You can not remove this comment type until you have removed the field.','','none'),(5261,_binary '%label is used by 1 comment on your site. You can not remove this comment type until you have removed all of the %label comments.%label is used by @count comments on your site. You may not remove %label until you have removed all of the %label comments.','','none'),(5262,_binary 'Translating configuration text','','none'),(5263,_binary 'Translating date formats','','none'),(5264,_binary 'This page lists all configuration items on your site that have translatable text, like your site name, role names, etc.','','11.3.8'),(5265,_binary 'Allow other users to contact you via a personal contact form which keeps your email address hidden. Note that some privileged users such as site administrators are still able to contact you even if you choose to disable this feature.','','11.3.8'),(5266,_binary 'Example: \'webmaster@example.com\' or \'sales@example.com,support@example.com\' . To specify multiple recipients, separate each email address with a comma.','','11.3.8'),(5267,_binary '%recipient is an invalid email address.','','none'),(5268,_binary '%sender-name (@sender-from) sent %recipient-name an email.','','none'),(5269,_binary 'Enabling field translation','','none'),(5270,_binary 'You can define which fields of a content entity can be translated. For example, you might want to translate the title and body field while leaving the image field untranslated. If you exclude a field from being translated, it will still show up in the content editing form, but any changes made to that field will be applied to <em>all</em> translations of that content.','','none'),(5271,_binary 'If translation is enabled you can translate a content entity via the Translate tab (or Translate link). The Translations page of a content entity gives an overview of the translation status for the current content and lets you add, edit, and delete its translations. This process is similar for every translatable content entity on your site.','','none'),(5272,_binary 'Changing the source language for a translation','','none'),(5273,_binary 'When you add a new translation, the original text you are translating is displayed in the edit form as the <em>source</em>. If at least one translation of the original content already exists when you add a new translation, you can choose either the original content (default) or one of the other translations as the source, using the select list in the Source language section. After saving the translation, the chosen source language is then listed on the Translate tab of the content.','','none'),(5274,_binary 'Setting status of translations','','none'),(5275,_binary 'If you edit a translation in one language you may want to set the status of the other translations as <em>out-of-date</em>. You can set this status by selecting the <em>Flag other translations as outdated</em> checkbox in the Translation section of the content editing form. The status will be visible on the Translations page.','','none'),(5276,_binary 'Managing and displaying date fields','','none'),(5277,_binary 'Displaying dates','','none'),(5278,_binary 'Jan','Abbreviated month name','none'),(5279,_binary 'Feb','Abbreviated month name','none'),(5280,_binary 'Mar','Abbreviated month name','11.3.8'),(5281,_binary 'Apr','Abbreviated month name','11.3.8'),(5282,_binary 'May','Abbreviated month name','11.3.8'),(5283,_binary 'Jun','Abbreviated month name','none'),(5284,_binary 'Jul','Abbreviated month name','none'),(5285,_binary 'Aug','Abbreviated month name','none'),(5286,_binary 'Sep','Abbreviated month name','none'),(5287,_binary 'Oct','Abbreviated month name','none'),(5288,_binary 'Nov','Abbreviated month name','none'),(5289,_binary 'Dec','Abbreviated month name','none'),(5290,_binary 'Sun','Abbreviated weekday','none'),(5291,_binary 'Mon','Abbreviated weekday','none'),(5292,_binary 'Tue','Abbreviated weekday','none'),(5293,_binary 'Wed','Abbreviated weekday','none'),(5294,_binary 'Thu','Abbreviated weekday','none'),(5295,_binary 'Fri','Abbreviated weekday','none'),(5296,_binary 'Sat','Abbreviated weekday','none'),(5297,_binary 'Su','Abbreviated weekday','none'),(5298,_binary 'Mo','Abbreviated weekday','none'),(5299,_binary 'Tu','Abbreviated weekday','none'),(5300,_binary 'We','Abbreviated weekday','none'),(5301,_binary 'Th','Abbreviated weekday','none'),(5302,_binary 'Fr','Abbreviated weekday','none'),(5303,_binary 'Sa','Abbreviated weekday','none'),(5304,_binary 'S','Abbreviated 1 letter weekday Sunday','none'),(5305,_binary 'M','Abbreviated 1 letter weekday Monday','none'),(5306,_binary 'T','Abbreviated 1 letter weekday Tuesday','none'),(5307,_binary 'W','Abbreviated 1 letter weekday Wednesday','none'),(5308,_binary 'T','Abbreviated 1 letter weekday Thursday','none'),(5309,_binary 'F','Abbreviated 1 letter weekday Friday','none'),(5310,_binary 'S','Abbreviated 1 letter weekday Saturday','none'),(5311,_binary 'Track images uploaded via a Text Editor','','none'),(5312,_binary 'The status of the file, temporary (FALSE) and permanent (TRUE).','','none'),(5313,_binary 'Web page addresses and email addresses turn into links automatically.','','11.3.8'),(5314,_binary 'Background color must be a hexadecimal color value.','','none'),(5315,_binary '(upscaling allowed)','','none'),(5316,_binary 'Adding languages','','none'),(5317,_binary 'Adding custom languages','','none'),(5318,_binary 'You can add a language that is not provided in the drop-down list by choosing <em>Custom language</em> at the end of the list. You then have to configure its language code, name, and direction in the form provided.','','none'),(5319,_binary 'Configuring content languages','','none'),(5320,_binary 'Adding a language switcher block','','none'),(5321,_binary 'Making a block visible per language','','none'),(5322,_binary 'Choosing user languages','','none'),(5323,_binary 'Users can choose a <em>Site language</em> on their profile page. This language is used for email messages, and can be used by modules to determine a user\'s language. It can also be used for interface text, if the <em>User</em> method is enabled as a <em>Detection and selection</em> method (see below). Administrative users can choose a separate <em>Administration pages language</em> for the interface text on administration pages. This configuration is only available on the user\'s profile page if the <em>Account administration pages</em> method is enabled (see below).','','none'),(5324,_binary '<em>URL</em> sets the interface language based on a path prefix or domain (for example specifying <em>de</em> for German would result in URLs like <em>example.com/de/contact</em>). The default language does not require a path prefix, but can have one assigned as well. If the language detection is done by domain name, a domain needs to be specified for each language.','','none'),(5325,_binary '<em>Session</em> determines the interface language from a request or session parameter (for example <em>example.com?language=de</em> would set the interface language to German based on the use of <em>de</em> as the <em>language</em> parameter).','','none'),(5326,_binary '<em>User</em> follows the language configuration set on the user\'s profile page.','','none'),(5327,_binary '<em>Account administration pages</em> follows the configuration set as <em>Administration pages language</em> on the profile page of an administrative user. This method is similar to the <em>User</em> method, but only sets the interface text language on administration pages, independent of the interface text language on other pages.','','none'),(5328,_binary '<em>Selected language</em> allows you to specify the site\'s default language or a specific language as the fall-back language. This method should be listed last.','','none'),(5329,_binary 'The comment author\'s email address from the comment form, if user is anonymous, and the \'Anonymous users may/must leave their contact information\' setting is turned on.','','none'),(5330,_binary 'Comma-separated list of recipient email addresses.','','none'),(5331,_binary 'Promote, change ownership, edit revisions, and perform other tasks across all content types.','','11.3.8'),(5332,_binary 'Syndicate block','','none'),(5333,_binary 'Use shortcuts','','11.3.8'),(5334,_binary 'Diff settings','','none'),(5335,_binary 'Number of leading lines in a diff','','none'),(5336,_binary 'Number of trailing lines in a diff','','none'),(5337,_binary 'Branding block','','none'),(5338,_binary 'Use site logo','','none'),(5339,_binary 'The current theme is not @theme','','none'),(5340,_binary 'The current theme is @theme','','none'),(5341,_binary 'Do not return true on the following pages: @pages','','none'),(5342,_binary 'Return true on the following pages: @pages','','none'),(5343,_binary 'Request Path','','none'),(5344,_binary 'Username or email address','','11.3.8'),(5345,_binary 'Email addresses to notify when updates are available','','none'),(5346,_binary 'Email notification threshold','','none'),(5347,_binary 'Whenever your site checks for available updates and finds new releases, it can notify a list of users via email. Put e