. It is possible to allow multiple media types in the same field.','','none'),(7158,_binary 'Differences between Media, File, and Image reference fields','','none'),(7159,_binary '<em>Media</em> reference fields offer several advantages over basic <em>File</em> and <em>Image</em> references:','','none'),(7160,_binary 'Media reference fields can reference multiple media types in the same field.','','none'),(7161,_binary 'Fields can also be added to media types themselves, which means that custom metadata like descriptions and taxonomy tags can be added for the referenced media. (Basic file and image fields do not support this.)','','none'),(7162,_binary 'Media types for audio and video files are provided by default, so there is no need for additional configuration to upload these media.','','none'),(7163,_binary 'Contributed or custom projects can provide additional media sources (such as third-party websites, Twitter, etc.).','','none'),(7164,_binary 'Existing media items can be reused on any other content items with a media reference field.','','none'),(7165,_binary 'For more information, see the <a href=\"@help_url\">Media help page</a>.','','11.3.8'),(7166,_binary 'Media Name','','none'),(7167,_binary '%type_name: Create new media','','11.3.8'),(7168,_binary '%type_name: Edit own media','','11.3.8'),(7169,_binary '%type_name: Edit any media','','11.3.8'),(7170,_binary '%type_name: Delete own media','','11.3.8'),(7171,_binary '%type_name: Delete any media','','11.3.8'),(7172,_binary '<em>The media source cannot be changed after the media type is created.</em>','','none'),(7173,_binary 'Use audio files for reusable media.','','none'),(7174,_binary 'Use video files for reusable media.','','none'),(7175,_binary 'The destination system contains data which was not created by a migration.','','none'),(7176,_binary 'Migrate Drupal settings','','none'),(7177,_binary 'source_module enforcement tags','','none'),(7178,_binary 'Old site','','none'),(7179,_binary 'The site you want to upgrade.','','none'),(7180,_binary 'New site','','none'),(7181,_binary 'Preparation steps','','none'),(7182,_binary 'WARNING: Content may be overwritten on your new site.','','none'),(7183,_binary 'I acknowledge I may lose data. Continue anyway.','','none'),(7184,_binary 'There is conflicting content of these types:','','none'),(7185,_binary 'On the <a href=\":cache-settings\">Performance page</a>, you can configure how long browsers and proxies may cache pages based on the Cache-Control header; this setting is ignored by the Internal Page Cache module, which caches pages permanently until invalidation, unless they carry an Expires header. There is no other configuration.','','none'),(7186,_binary 'The Settings Tray module allows users with the <a href=\":administer_block_permission\">Administer blocks</a> and <a href=\":contextual_permission\">Use contextual links</a> permissions to edit blocks without visiting a separate page. For more information, see the <a href=\":handbook_url\">online documentation for the Settings Tray module</a>.','','none'),(7187,_binary 'Editing blocks in place','','none'),(7188,_binary 'To edit blocks in place, either click the <strong>Edit</strong> button in the toolbar and then click on the block, or choose \"Quick edit\" from the block\'s contextual link. (See the <a href=\":contextual\">Contextual Links module help</a> for more information about how to use contextual links.)','','none'),(7189,_binary 'The Settings Tray for the block will open in a sidebar, with a compact form for configuring what the block shows.','','none'),(7190,_binary 'Save the form and the changes will be immediately visible on the page.','','none'),(7191,_binary 'Specify the format of the syslog entry. Available variables are: <dl><dt><code>!base_url</code></dt><dd>Base URL of the site.</dd><dt><code>!timestamp</code></dt><dd>Unix timestamp of the log entry.</dd><dt><code>!type</code></dt><dd>The category to which this message belongs.</dd><dt><code>!ip</code></dt><dd>IP address of the user triggering the message.</dd><dt><code>!request_uri</code></dt><dd>The requested URI.</dd><dt><code>!referer</code></dt><dd>HTTP Referer if available.</dd><dt><code>!severity</code></dt><dd>The severity level of the event; ranges from 0 (Emergency) to 7 (Debug).</dd><dt><code>!uid</code></dt><dd>User ID.</dd><dt><code>!link</code></dt><dd>A link to associate with the message.</dd><dt><code>!message</code></dt><dd>The message to store in the log.</dd></dl>','','none'),(7192,_binary 'Either the path \'%path\' is invalid or you do not have access to it.','','none'),(7193,_binary '%capital_name contains the following terms.','','none'),(7194,_binary '%capital_name contains terms grouped under parent terms','','none'),(7195,_binary '%capital_name contains terms with multiple parents.','','none'),(7196,_binary 'Access the taxonomy vocabulary overview page','','11.3.8'),(7197,_binary 'Get an overview of all taxonomy vocabularies.','','11.3.8'),(7198,_binary '%vocabulary: Create terms','','11.3.8'),(7199,_binary '%vocabulary: Delete terms','','11.3.8'),(7200,_binary '%vocabulary: Edit terms','','11.3.8'),(7201,_binary 'Output the URL as text','','11.3.8'),(7202,_binary 'Output an absolute link','','none'),(7203,_binary 'Min placeholder','','none'),(7204,_binary 'Max placeholder','','none'),(7205,_binary 'Enable this option to output an absolute link. Required if you want to use the path as a link destination.','','11.3.8'),(7206,_binary 'Enforce a <code>destination</code> parameter in the link to return the user to the original view upon completing the link action. Most operations include a destination by default and this setting is no longer needed.','','none'),(7207,_binary 'Hint text that appears inside the Min field when empty.','','none'),(7208,_binary 'Hint text that appears inside the Max field when empty.','','none'),(7209,_binary 'Hint text that appears inside the field when empty.','','none'),(7210,_binary 'There are no workflow types available. In order to create workflows you need to install a module that provides a workflow type. For example, the <a href=\":content-moderation\">Content Moderation</a> module provides a workflow type that enables workflows for content entities.','','none'),(7211,_binary 'Transition label','','none'),(7212,_binary 'A locally hosted audio file.','','11.3.8'),(7213,_binary 'A locally hosted video file.','','11.3.8'),(7214,_binary 'Workspace name','','none'),(7215,_binary 'Name (A-Z)','','11.3.8'),(7216,_binary 'A flag indicating whether this was a default revision when it was saved.','','11.3.8'),(7217,_binary 'Entity untranslatable fields','Validation','none'),(7218,_binary 'The Content Moderation module allows you to expand on Drupal\'s \"unpublished\" and \"published\" states for content. It allows you to have a published version that is live, but have a separate working copy that is undergoing review before it is published. This is achieved by using <a href=\":workflows\">Workflows</a> to apply different states and transitions to entities as needed. For more information, see the <a href=\":content_moderation\">online documentation for the Content Moderation module</a>.','','none'),(7219,_binary 'Applying workflows','','none'),(7220,_binary 'Moderating content','','none'),(7221,_binary 'You can view a list of content awaiting moderation on the <a href=\":moderated\">moderated content page</a>. This will show any content in an unpublished state, such as Draft or Archived, to help surface content that requires more work from content editors.','','none'),(7222,_binary 'Each transition is exposed as a permission. If a user has the permission for a transition, they can use the transition to change the state of the content item, from Draft to Published.','','none'),(7223,_binary 'Hide non translatable fields on translation forms','','11.3.8'),(7224,_binary 'Content translation bundle settings','','none'),(7225,_binary 'Bundle settings values','','none'),(7226