 <em>Save blocks</em>.','','11.3.8'),(7824,_binary 'If you want to change additional settings, find the region where the block you want to update is currently located, and click <em>Configure</em> in the line of the block description.','','11.3.8'),(7825,_binary 'Edit the block\'s settings. The available settings vary depending on the module that provides the block, but for all blocks you can change:','','11.3.8'),(7826,_binary '<em>Block title</em>: The heading for the block on your site -- for some blocks, you will need to check the <em>Override title</em> checkbox in order to enter a title','','11.3.8'),(7827,_binary '<em>Display title</em>: Check the box if you want the title displayed','','11.3.8'),(7828,_binary '<em>Visibility</em>: Add conditions for when the block should be displayed','','11.3.8'),(7829,_binary '<em>Region</em>: Change the theme region the block is displayed in','','11.3.8'),(7830,_binary 'Click <em>Save block</em>.','','11.3.8'),(7831,_binary 'What are blocks?','','11.3.8'),(7832,_binary 'Blocks are boxes of content rendered into an area, or region, of a web page of your site. Blocks are placed and configured specifically for each theme.','','11.3.8'),(7833,_binary 'What is the block description?','','11.3.8'),(7834,_binary 'The block description is an identification name for a block, which is shown in the administrative interface. It is not displayed on the site.','','11.3.8'),(7835,_binary 'What is the block title?','','11.3.8'),(7836,_binary 'The block title is the heading that is optionally shown to site visitors when the block is placed in a region.','','11.3.8'),(7837,_binary 'Place a block into a theme\'s region.','','11.3.8'),(7838,_binary 'Click the name of the theme that you want to place the block in.','','11.3.8'),(7839,_binary 'Find the region where you want the block, and click <em>Place block</em> in that region. A modal dialog will pop up.','','11.3.8'),(7840,_binary 'Find the block you want to place and click <em>Place block</em>. A <em>Configure block</em> modal dialog will pop up.','','11.3.8'),(7841,_binary 'Enter a description of your block (to be shown to administrators) and the body text for your block.','','11.3.8'),(7842,_binary 'Enter a label for this block type (shown in the administrative interface). Optionally, edit the automatically-generated machine name or the description.','','11.3.8'),(7843,_binary 'Click <em>Save</em>. You will be returned to the <em>Block types</em> page.','','11.3.8'),(7844,_binary 'Click <em>Manage fields</em> in the row of your new block type, and add the desired fields to your block type.','','11.3.8'),(7845,_binary 'Use contextual links to access administrative tasks without navigating the administrative menu.','','11.3.8'),(7846,_binary 'What are contextual links?','','11.3.8'),(7847,_binary 'Visit a non-administrative page on your site, such as the home page.','','11.3.8'),(7848,_binary 'Locate a block or another area on the page that you want to edit or configure.','','11.3.8'),(7849,_binary 'Complete your administrative task and save your settings, or cancel the action. You should be returned to the page you started from.','','11.3.8'),(7850,_binary 'What are security updates?','','11.3.8'),(7851,_binary 'Any software occasionally has bugs, and sometimes these bugs have security implications. When security bugs are fixed in the core software, modules, or themes that your site uses, they are released in a <em>security update</em>. You will need to apply security updates in order to keep your site secure.','','11.3.8'),(7852,_binary 'Security tasks','','11.3.8'),(7853,_binary 'Overview of accessibility','','11.3.8'),(7854,_binary 'The core Shortcuts module enhances the toolbar with a configurable list of links to commonly-used tasks.','','11.3.8'),(7855,_binary 'If you install the core Contextual Links module, non-administrative pages will contain links leading to related administrative tasks.','','11.3.8'),(7856,_binary 'The core Help module displays help topics, and provides a Help block that can be placed on administrative pages to provide an overview of their functionality.','','11.3.8'),(7857,_binary 'See the related topics listed below for specific tasks.','','11.3.8'),(7858,_binary 'Set up your site so that users can search for help.','','11.3.8'),(7859,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Search and metadata</em> &gt; <em>Search pages</em>.','','11.3.8'),(7860,_binary 'Verify that a Help search page is listed in the <em>Search pages</em> section. If not, add a new page of type <em>Help</em>.','','11.3.8'),(7861,_binary 'Create, view, and use a set of shortcuts to access administrative pages.','','11.3.8'),(7862,_binary 'What are shortcuts?','','11.3.8'),(7863,_binary '<em>Shortcuts</em> are quick links to administrative pages; they are managed by the core Shortcut module. A site can have one or more <em>shortcut sets</em>, which can be shared by one or more users (by default, there is only one set shared by all users); each set contains a limited number of shortcuts. Users need <em>Use shortcuts</em> permission to view shortcuts; <em>Edit current shortcut set</em> permission to add, delete, or edit the shortcuts in the set assigned to them; and <em>Select any shortcut set</em> permission to select a different shortcut set when editing their user profile. There is also an <em>Administer shortcuts</em> permission, which allows an administrator to do any of these actions, as well as select shortcut sets for other users.','','11.3.8'),(7864,_binary 'Navigate to an administrative page that you want in your shortcut list.','','11.3.8'),(7865,_binary 'Repeat until all the desired links have been added to your shortcut set.','','11.3.8'),(7866,_binary 'Click any link in the shortcut bar to go directly to the administrative page.','','11.3.8'),(7867,_binary 'Configure the basic settings of your site, including the site name, slogan, main email address, default time zone, default country, and the date formats to use.','','11.3.8'),(7868,_binary 'Enter the site name, slogan, and main email address for your site.','','11.3.8'),(7869,_binary 'Select the default country and default time zone for your site.','','11.3.8'),(7870,_binary 'Set up your site to respond appropriately to site errors, including 403 and 404 page responses.','','11.3.8'),(7871,_binary 'What are 403 and 404 responses?','','11.3.8'),(7872,_binary 'What other errors can occur?','','11.3.8'),(7873,_binary 'If desired, create pages to use for 403 and 404 responses. Note the URLs for these pages.','','11.3.8'),(7874,_binary 'Configure settings related to how user accounts are created and deleted.','','11.3.8'),(7875,_binary 'What are the settings related to user account creation and deletion?','','11.3.8'),(7876,_binary 'You can edit the email messages that are sent to users when their accounts are pending, approved, created, blocked, or canceled, or when they request a password reset.','','11.3.8'),(7877,_binary '[site:login-url]: The URL where users can log in to your site.','','11.3.8'),(7878,_binary '[user:display-name]: The user\'s displayed name.','','11.3.8'),(7879,_binary 'Verify that the other settings are correct.','','11.3.8'),(7880,_binary 'Topics can be provided by modules or themes. Top-level help topics on your site:','','none'),(7881,_binary 'Provides the API allowing to rename URLs.','','none'),(7882,_binary 'The parent workspace.','','none'),(7883,_binary 'Merge workspace','','none'),(7884,_binary 'Only top-level workspaces can be published.','','none'),(7885,_binary 'Merge into @target_label','','none'),(7886,_binary 'The %label workspace can not be deleted because it has child workspaces.','','none'),(7887,_binary 'There are no changes that can be merged from %source_label to %target_label.','','none'),(7888,_binary 'Would you like to merge the contents of the %source_label workspace into %target_label?','','none'),(7889,_bin