n','','11.3.8'),(11226,_binary 'Administer Mail System','','11.3.8'),(11227,_binary 'Administer meta tags','','11.3.8'),(11228,_binary 'Administer Minify HTML Module','','11.3.8'),(11229,_binary 'Administer pathauto','','11.3.8'),(11230,_binary 'Bulk delete aliases','','11.3.8'),(11231,_binary 'Bulk update aliases','','11.3.8'),(11232,_binary 'Notify of Path Changes','','11.3.8'),(11233,_binary 'Administer Security Kit','','11.3.8'),(11234,_binary 'Administer sitemap settings','','11.3.8'),(11235,_binary 'Edit entity sitemap settings','','11.3.8'),(11236,_binary 'This field is required.','','11.3.8'),(11237,_binary 'Minified Source HTML.','','11.3.8'),(11238,_binary 'Toggle minified HTML on or off.','','11.3.8'),(11239,_binary 'Strip comments from the source HTML','','11.3.8'),(11240,_binary 'If checked, strip HTML comments and multi-line comments in @script and @style tags.','','11.3.8'),(11241,_binary 'Disable minification for specific pages','','11.3.8'),(11242,_binary 'Specify pages by using their paths with leading forward slash. Enter one path per line. The \'*\' character is a wildcard. Example paths are %blog for the blog page and %blog-wildcard for every personal blog. %front is the front page.','','11.3.8'),(11243,_binary 'Specify the existing path you wish to alias. For example: /node/28, /media/1, /taxonomy/term/1.','','11.3.8'),(11244,_binary 'La ruta de orígen debería comenzar con una barra diagonal.','','11.3.8'),(11245,_binary 'El alias de la ruta tiene que empezar con una barra diagonal.','','11.3.8'),(11246,_binary 'Duplicate Pathauto pattern','','11.3.8'),(11247,_binary 'Select the types of paths for which to generate URL aliases','','11.3.8'),(11248,_binary 'Generate a URL alias for un-aliased paths only','','11.3.8'),(11249,_binary 'Update the URL alias for paths having an old URL alias','','11.3.8'),(11250,_binary 'Regenerate URL aliases for all paths','','11.3.8'),(11251,_binary 'Select which URL aliases to generate','','11.3.8'),(11252,_binary 'Bulk generation can be used to generate URL aliases for items that currently have no aliases. This is typically used when installing Pathauto on a site that has existing un-aliased content that needs to be aliased in bulk.','','11.3.8'),(11253,_binary 'It can also be used to regenerate URL aliases for items that have an old alias and for which the Pathauto pattern has been changed.','','11.3.8'),(11254,_binary 'Note that this will only affect items which are configured to have their URL alias automatically set. Items whose URL alias is manually set are not affected.','','11.3.8'),(11255,_binary 'Bulk updating URL aliases','','11.3.8'),(11256,_binary 'Updated alias for %label @id.','','11.3.8'),(11257,_binary 'No new URL aliases to generate.','','11.3.8'),(11258,_binary 'YouTube video ID: @video_id','','11.3.8'),(11259,_binary 'Sitemaps can be regenerated on demand here.','','11.3.8'),(11260,_binary '@indexed out of @total queue items have been processed.<br>Each sitemap is published after all of its items have been processed.','','11.3.8'),(11261,_binary 'Rebuild queue','','11.3.8'),(11262,_binary 'Rebuild queue & generate','','11.3.8'),(11263,_binary 'Progress of sitemap regeneration','','11.3.8'),(11264,_binary 'Sitemap status','','11.3.8'),(11265,_binary 'Link count','','11.3.8'),(11266,_binary 'published on @time','','11.3.8'),(11267,_binary 'Add sitemap','','11.3.8'),(11268,_binary 'Include this sitemap during generation','','11.3.8'),(11269,_binary 'The sitemap ID will be part of the URL and can only contain lowercase letters, numbers, dashes and underscores.','','11.3.8'),(11270,_binary 'Sitemap type','','11.3.8'),(11271,_binary 'The sitemap\'s type defines its looks and content. Sitemaps types can be configured <a href=\"@url\">here</a>.','','11.3.8'),(11272,_binary 'Regenerate the sitemaps during cron runs','','11.3.8'),(11273,_binary 'Uncheck this if you intend to only regenerate the sitemaps manually or via drush.','','11.3.8'),(11274,_binary 'On every cron run','','11.3.8'),(11275,_binary 'Sitemap generation interval','','11.3.8'),(11276,_binary 'The sitemap will be generated according to this interval.','','11.3.8'),(11277,_binary 'Add styling and sorting to sitemaps','','11.3.8'),(11278,_binary 'If checked, sitemaps will be displayed as tables with sortable entries and thus become much friendlier towards human visitors. Search engines will not care.','','11.3.8'),(11279,_binary 'Hide branding','','11.3.8'),(11280,_binary 'Remove the \'Generated by the Simple XML Sitemap Drupal module\' string from the XSL output.','','11.3.8'),(11281,_binary 'Remove hreflang markup in HTML','','11.3.8'),(11282,_binary 'Google recommends displaying hreflang definitions either in the HTML markup or in the sitemap, but not in both places.<br>If checked, hreflang definitions created by the language module will be removed from the markup reducing its size.','','11.3.8'),(11283,_binary 'Skip non-existent translations','','11.3.8'),(11284,_binary 'If checked, entity links are generated exclusively for languages the entity has been translated to as long as the language is not excluded below.<br>Otherwise entity links are generated for every language installed on the site apart from languages excluded below.<br>Bear in mind that non-entity paths like homepage will always be generated for every non-excluded language.','','11.3.8'),(11285,_binary 'Exclude languages','','11.3.8'),(11286,_binary 'There will be no links generated for languages checked here.','','11.3.8'),(11287,_binary 'Default sitemap','','11.3.8'),(11288,_binary 'This sitemap will be available under <em>/sitemap.xml</em> in addition to its default path <em>/variant-name/sitemap.xml</em>.<br>Sitemaps can be configured <a href=\"@url\">here</a>.','','11.3.8'),(11289,_binary 'On some hosting providers it is impossible to pass parameters to cron to tell Drupal which URL to bootstrap with. In this case the base URL of sitemap links can be overridden here.<br>Example: <em>@url</em>','','11.3.8'),(11290,_binary 'Exclude duplicate links','','11.3.8'),(11291,_binary 'Prevent per-sitemap duplicate links.<br>Unchecking this may help avoiding PHP memory errors on huge sites.','','11.3.8'),(11292,_binary 'Maximum links in a sitemap','','11.3.8'),(11293,_binary 'The maximum number of links one sitemap can hold. If more links are generated than set here, a sitemap index will be created and the links split into several sub-sitemaps.<br>50 000 links is the maximum Google will parse per sitemap, but choosing a lower value may be needed to avoid PHP memory errors on huge sites.<br>If left blank, all links will be shown on a single sitemap.','','11.3.8'),(11294,_binary 'Sitemap generation max duration','','11.3.8'),(11295,_binary 'The maximum duration <strong>in seconds</strong> the generation task can run during a single cron run or during one batch process iteration.<br>The higher the number, the quicker the generation process, but higher the risk of PHP timeout errors.','','11.3.8'),(11296,_binary 'Entities per queue item','','11.3.8'),(11297,_binary 'The number of entities to process in each queue item.<br>Increasing this number will use more memory but will result in less queries improving generation speed.','','11.3.8'),(11298,_binary 'Default sitemap generator','','11.3.8'),(11299,_binary 'Custom URL generator','','11.3.8'),(11300,_binary 'Entity URL generator','','11.3.8'),(11301,_binary 'Menu link URL generator','','11.3.8'),(11302,_binary 'Arbitrary URL generator','','11.3.8'),(11303,_binary 'Sitemap index generator','','11.3.8'),(11304,_binary 'Sitemap URL generator','','11.3.8'),(11305,_binary 'Sitemap generator','','11.3.8'),(11306,_binary 'URL generators','','11.3.8'),(11307,_binary 'Add sitemap type','','11.3.8'),(11308,_binary 'Sitemaps of this type will be built according to the sitemap generator plugin chosen here.','','11.3.8'),(11309,_binary 'Sitemaps of this type will be populated with URLs generated by these URL generator plugins.','','11.3.8'),(11310,_binary 'Indexed bundles','','11.3.8'),(11311,_binary 'Simple XML Sitemap settings will be added only to entity forms of entity types enabled here. Settings for specific entity bundles (e.g. <em>page</em>) can be adjusted here or on the bundle pages.','','11.3.8'),(11312,_binary 'The sitemap settings and any per-entity overrides will be deleted for the unchecked entity types.','','11.3.8'),(11313,_binary 'Configure %label entity type','','11.3.8'),(11314,_binary 'The generation failed to finish. It can be continued manually on the module\'s settings page, or via drush.','','11.3.8'),(11315,_binary 'Generating XML sitemaps','','11.3.8'),(11316,_binary 'Processing items from the queue.<br>Each sitemap gets published after all of its items have been processed.','','11.3.8'),(11317,_binary '@indexed out of @total total queue items have been processed.','','11.3.8'),(11318,_binary '%bundle_label <span class=\"description\">(sitemaps: %sitemaps)</span>','','11.3.8'),(11319,_binary 'If a custom link points to an entity, include its referenced images in the sitemap.','','11.3.8'),(11320,_binary 'Add custom internal drupal paths to specific sitemaps.','','11.3.8'),(11321,_binary 'Specify drupal internal (relative) paths, one per line. Do not forget to prepend the paths with a \'/\'.<br>Optionally link priority <em>(0.0 - 1.0)</em> can be added by appending it after a space.<br> Optionally link change frequency <em>(always / hourly / daily / weekly / monthly / yearly / never)</em> can be added by appending it after a space.','','11.3.8'),(11322,_binary '<strong>Examples:</strong><br><em>/ 1.0 daily</em> -> home page with the highest priority and daily change frequency<br><em>/contact</em> -> contact page with the default priority and no change frequency information','','11.3.8'),(11323,_binary 'Generated by the <a href=\"@url\">@module_name</a> Drupal module.','','11.3.8'),(11324,_binary 'Meta tag patterns are passed down from one level to the next unless they are overridden. To view a summary of the individual meta tags and the pattern for a specific configuration, click on its name below.','','11.3.8');
